Description: hw/arm: Add the i.MX21 SoC
 An ARM926EJ-S (r0p4) with the i.MX21's interrupt controller, GPT1-3
 timers, UART1-4 (the existing i.MX serial model), clock and reset
 module, GPIO ports, CSPI1-3, LCD and NAND flash controllers, PWM,
 keypad port, DMA controller, SSI1-2 and AUDMUX (with their interrupts
 and DMA request lines), USB host, watchdog, RTC and I2C controller.
 Peripheral and memory controller registers that are not modelled read
 back what was written.
 .
 The stock Chumby kernel uses the watchdog: chumby_sense1 arms it with a
 2.5 second timeout (WCR 0x0434) and services it from a timer every
 tick, arch_reset() reboots through it (WCR = WDE with SRS clear), and
 /proc/resetReason reports WRSR as read at start-up. The i.MX21 block is
 the i.MX2 watchdog (16-bit WCR, WSR, WRSR at 0x10002000, IRQ 27), so it
 is imx2.wdt with its reset-source property set, and a stall grace of
 250 ms so that a host that stops running QEMU for a while doesn't reset
 the guest. A missed service performs QEMU's watchdog action and
 "reboot" resets the machine.
 .
 The RTC (0x10007000, IRQ 22) and the I2C controller (0x10012000, IRQ 12,
 the i.MX1-style block of imx.i2c) are there for kernels that drive them.
 The stock kernel does not: it is built without CONFIG_RTC and
 CONFIG_I2C_IMX, and mx21ads.c keeps the OTG transceiver set-up, which
 used the USB OTG block's own I2C master, under "#if 0". The I2C bus is
 empty; devices can be added to it with -device.
 .
 The SDHC is not modelled: the Chumby Classic has no card slot, its
 board file keeps imx_set_mmc_info() under "#if 0" and the kernel is
 built without CONFIG_MMC.
